# --- publishing allowlist -------------------------------------------------
# The repo root doubles as a working directory for ad-hoc analysis: ~130 one-off scripts,
# figures, and multi-GB data archives (EGRET_TWAS_association_results.tar.gz alone is 1.1 GB,
# well past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit). Publish only the pipeline: ignore everything at
# the top level, then re-admit the tracked files and the two code directories. New root-level
# clutter is ignored by default; to publish something new, add a `!` line for it.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/environment.yml
!/post_install.R
!/scripts/
!/grn_analysis_files/

# Keep new GRN data and ad-hoc helpers out by default. Already tracked files remain tracked;
# these exceptions admit the stage-9 chain and converter when cloning or rebuilding the index.
/grn_analysis_files/*
!/grn_analysis_files/9.2_identify_trans_regulators.py
!/grn_analysis_files/9.3_assign_trans_regulators_with_eqtl.py
!/grn_analysis_files/9.4_determine_grns.py
!/grn_analysis_files/9.5_average_z_score_module.R
!/grn_analysis_files/convert_variant_id_to_rsid.py

scripts/*.ipynb
scripts/CLAUDE.md
